{"text": "Randall Franke\n\nrfranke@opendoorslic.com\n503-559-0872\nJanuary 2008\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE:\nFranke & Associates, Owner present\nProviding consultation and project management \u2014 specializing in governmental affairs, non-profit\nmanagement, fundraising, facilitation, communication, strategic planning, and advocacy.\n\nOpen Doors Consulting, Founding Principal present\nRecognizing that government has a direct impact on the lives of the people they serve and that business can\nplay an integral role in meeting those needs, ODC Helps Business Help Government Serve People.\n\nCommissioner, Marion County 1979 \u2014 2003\nElected to six four-year terms on a full-time, three-member board responsible for setting policies, procedures\nand budget for all county functions and day-to-day operations of non-elected departments. Served on numerous\nnational, regional, state, and local boards and commissions. In addition, was the lead on many notable projects\nwhich saved taxpayer dollars, put criminals behind bars and protected our environment. Elected President of\nNational Association of Counties and Association of Oregon Counties and served on various committees within\nboth organizations. Frequent guest speaker, panelist and moderator at numerous national and state programs\ninvolving solid waste management, children and family issues and local collaborative community planning.\n\nManager, Marion County Risk Management Program 1974 \u2014 1979\nResearched, analyzed, and recommended establishment of Marion County\u2019s first risk management program to\ncomply with 1973 Oregon Safe Employment Act. Developed self-insurance program that cut loss time\naccidents and liability exposure and saved more than $1 million a year.\n\nEDUCATION\nUniversity of Oregon, BS, 1969\nWestern Oregon University, MS, 1974\nHarvard University, 1980\nJohn F. Kennedy School of Government \u2014 Three-week program for executive level decision-makers in\nstate, county and municipal government.\nAmerican Leadership Forum, 1987-1988\nYearlong interactive program to develop individual interpersonal skills, organizational, communication,\nand grass roots leadership skills.\nPacific Program, 1989\nWeeklong training to develop analytical, communication, and interpersonal skills for effective policy\nleadership and public management.\n\nMILITARY SERVICE:\nLt. j g U.S. Navy flight program, Honorable Discharge\n\nNATIONAL SERVICE:\nNational Association of Counties Board of Directors 1998-2003, President 1994-1995\nThe Finance Project Board of Directors 1996-2007\nEnvironmental Protection Agency, Local Government Advisory Committee 1995-1999, Chair 1995-1997\nPresident\u2019s Council on Sustainable Development 1997-1998 (Appointed by Pres Clinton)\nU.S. Advisory Commission in Intergovernmental Relations (ACIR) 1995-1996 (Appointed by Pres Clinton)\nThe Conservation Foundation 1989-1990\nLocal Government Solid Waste Action Coalition (SWAC) Co-Chair 1990-1993\n\nGOVERNOR APPOINTMENTS:\nLand Conservation and Development Commission (LCDC) 1995-2003, Chair 2002-2003\nState Commission on Children and Families Vice Chair 1993-1997\nWillamette Valley Livability Forum Advisory Board 1996-2000\nGovernor\u2019s Oregon Shines Task Force 1996-1997",
